research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-completeness-limits.provenance.jsonl:22:{"id":"ex-rational-function-field-order","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://math.hws.edu/eck/math331/guide2020/04-axioms-for-R.html"],"rationale":"The source defines positivity in the real rational-function field by the sign of the leading coefficient after normalizing the denominator, proves closure under addition and multiplication, and shows that t exceeds every canonical natural. This is exactly the local eventual-positive-infinity order; the local proof expands representative independence and the infinitesimal 1/t.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-completeness-limits.provenance.jsonl-23-{"id":"ex-field-ordered-in-two-ways","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"established-knowledge","urls":[],"rationale":"ESCALATED TO ALPHA. The two orders on Q(sqrt(2)) obtained from the two real embeddings are a standard algebraic example, and the local proof also shows these are the only two. Searches surfaced informal exact discussions but no reputable source among the allowed classes for the full exact package; this is established mathematics, not an invented construction. ALPHA CONCURRENCE: The current construction is the canonical quadratic-field ordering argument: the two real embeddings send sqrt(2) to its two conjugates, and every field order is fixed by the sign of that generator. This is standard established ordered-field mathematics, merely packaged locally.","alpha_concurred":true,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-completeness-limits.provenance.jsonl-24-{"id":"ex-cauchy-complete-not-complete-field","statement":"ai-generated","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"none","urls":[],"rationale":"Positive novelty determination: the exact property inventory for this library’s K=R((t^{-1})) is a bespoke composition rather than an established named result. Its ordered-field, Cauchy-complete, non-Archimedean, non-LUB, shrinking-NIP, non-BW, and non-MCT assertions follow from the source-backed local Laurent and completeness results cited in the item.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-completeness-limits.provenance.jsonl-25-{"id":"ex-cesaro-means-of-alternating","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ces%C3%A0ro_summation","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grandi%27s_series"],"rationale":"The sources give Cesaro averaging and the classical alternating pattern. The local item uses the term sequence 1,-1,... rather than Grandi partial sums, changes the Cesaro value accordingly to 0, and writes out the parity computation.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-completeness-limits.provenance.jsonl-26-{"id":"ex-stolz-cesaro-applied","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Faulhaber%27s_formula","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stolz%E2%80%93Ces%C3%A0ro_theorem"],"rationale":"The local example composes two sourced results rather than reproducing one source statement: Faulhaber’s formula gives leading term n^(p+1)/(p+1), hence the displayed limit, and Stolz-Cesaro supplies the stated difference-quotient route. The local proof expands the power factorization.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-completeness-limits.provenance.jsonl-27-{"id":"cex-q-not-dense-in-an-ordered-field","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Archimedean_property","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ordered_field"],"rationale":"The sources state that a non-Archimedean ordered field has infinitesimal intervals containing no rational and give R(t) as the standard example. The local witness fixes the interval (0,1/t) and verifies it from the canonical embedding.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-completeness-limits.provenance.jsonl-28-{"id":"cex-evt-and-ivt-fail-over-a-non-complete-field","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"established-knowledge","urls":[],"rationale":"ESCALATED TO ALPHA. Failure of IVT and EVT over Q through the missing root sqrt(2), including unbounded reciprocal and unattained extremum witnesses, is standard analysis over an incomplete ordered field. Searches found the component theorems but no allowed reputable source for this exact three-function package; it is established mathematics, not positively novel. ALPHA CONCURRENCE: The current three witnesses are canonical consequences of the missing rational root of x^2-2: x^2-2 misses an intermediate value, its negative square has an unattained supremum, and its reciprocal is unbounded. The bundled presentation is local, but the mathematics is standard and established.","alpha_concurred":true,"at":"2026-08-08"}
